---
title: Raspberry Pinwheels
course: Dessert
tags: 
 - Cookies
 - vegan
source: Modified from The Cookie Book
servings: 32
---

Preheat an oven to 350°F.

In a #Mixing bowl{} beat the @vegan butter{125%grams} with an #electric mixer{} on medium to high speed for ~{30%seconds}. Add the @sugar{100%g}, @plant-based milk{40%g}, @cornstarch{20%g}, and @baking powder{1%tsp}; beat until combined. Beat in the @vanilla{1%tsp}. Beat in as much of the @all-purpose flour{250%g} as you can with the mixer. Stir in any remaining flour with a #wooden spoon{}. Divide the dough in half. Cover and chill for about ~{3%hours}, or until it is easy to handle. 

On a lightly floured surface, roll each half of the dough into a 10-inch square (using a sharp knife, trim to exact dimensions). Using a #sharp knife{}, cut each square into sixteen 2.5 inch squares. Place 1/2 inch apart on ungreased #baking sheets{}. Cut 1-inch slits from each corner to center. Drop {1/2%tsp} of the @seedless jam{80%ml}(raspberry, strawberry, cranberry work well) in each center. Fold every other tip to the center to form a pinwheel. Press firmly to seal.

Bake for ~{8-10%minutes}, or until the edges are firm and lightly browned. Cool on baking sheets for ~{1%minute}. Remove cookies from the baking sheets and transfer to a #?wire rack{} to cool, if you have one. 